hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19241","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir meaning the brother of Amr ibn Muhajir narrated to us, he said: Aqil ibn Shabib narrated to me from Abu Wahb al-Jushami, and he had companionship, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with the names of the prophets. The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman, the truest are Harith and Hammam, and the ugliest are Harb and Murrah. Tie horses, wipe their forelocks and rumps, or he said: Their croups, put halters on them and do not halter them with strings. Keep to every dark bay blaze-faced white-stocked, or chestnut blaze-faced white-stocked, or black blaze-faced white-stocked."
"19242","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, Aqil ibn Shabib narrated to us from Abu Wahb al-Kalai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned its meaning. Muhammad said: I do not know whether he began with the dark bay or the black. They asked him: Why did he prefer the chestnut? He said: Because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and the first to come with victory was the rider of the chestnut."
